# Package activation examples

This package's extensions are runtime-disabled by default. Use `pi config` to select extensions interactively. For a deterministic settings-file activation, list the extension directory directly in Pi's global (`~/.pi/agent/settings.json`) or trusted project (`.pi/settings.json`) `extensions` array.

## Enable one extension (then opt it in at runtime)

Replace `/path/to/pi-packages` with the installed package directory. For npm and git packages, this is the installed package directory shown by `pi list`/`pi config`, not the source specifier.

```json
{
  "extensions": ["/path/to/pi-packages/extensions/file-guard"]
}
```
```

Choose one of these exact paths:

- `extensions/file-guard/index.ts`
- `extensions/mcp-client/index.ts`
- `extensions/workers/index.ts`

## Enable all bundled extensions (then opt each in at runtime)

```json
{
  "extensions": [
    "/path/to/pi-packages/extensions/file-guard",
    "/path/to/pi-packages/extensions/mcp-client",
    "/path/to/pi-packages/extensions/workers"
  ]
}
```

The extension-specific runtime opt-ins must also be configured: enable File Guard in its config/environment, set `enabled: true` in `.pi/workers.json`, and set `enabled: true` in MCP Client configuration.